# Claude Code Instructions

This project uses the **Meaningful Human Control** (MHC) methodology.

## Session Start

**At the start of every Claude Code session**, before the user types anything:

1. Read `../MHC-W/CLAUDE.md` — gives you the command set, architecture, version, and routing
2. Read `../MHC-W/router.md` — gives you the artifact chain and your role in maintained control

Do this **silently**. Do not announce "loading MHC…" unless something requires user attention (missing config, handoff file found, etc.).

## MHC Commands

When user types any MHC-* command, read `../MHC-W/CLAUDE.md` for routing, then the appropriate agent file.

**Shorthand:** `mhc` = `MHC-start`. Do not attempt it as a shell command.

## Available Commands

| Command       | Purpose                                              |
| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| `MHC-start`   | Initialize session, configure export, show workflows |
| `MHC-trace`   | Create epistemic trace (Brainstorm)                  |
| `MHC-PDL`     | Create prompt development log (Design)               |
| `MHC-prompt`  | Generate complete prompt (Design)                    |
| `MHC-modlog`  | Create modification log entry (Refine)               |
| `MHC-note`    | Capture to notes desktop                             |
| `MHC-status`  | Show project status, resume workflows                |
| `MHC-guide`   | Show methodology guide                               |
| `MHC-tools`   | List all commands                                    |
| `MHC-adapt`   | Learn about workflow adaptation                      |
| `MHC-handoff` | Generate portable handoff artifact                   |
| `MHC-resume`  | Collaborator entry point                             |
| `MHC-recover` | Export current conversation (Claude Code)            |
| `MHC-end`     | Wrap up session (Web mode)                           |
| `MHC-import`  | Import external conversation                         |
| `MHC-harvest` | Extract artifacts from conversation                  |

